@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# Qwen3.5 cache precision
+
+Qwen3.5 GDN has three independent precision settings. Its cache recipe records
+these dtypes in the memory plan; the arena creates typed views directly from
+that plan, without runtime casts to repair mismatches.
+
+| Cache field | Precision source | Default behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Conv history | Declared activation dtype, `AttnConfig.dtype` | BF16 activations retain BF16 history |
+| Recurrent SSM state | `TOKENSPEED_MAMBA_SSM_DTYPE`, published from `--mamba-ssm-dtype` | FP32; BF16 remains an explicit alternative |
+| Full-attention K/V | `--kv-cache-dtype` / Python `kv_cache_dtype` | `auto` still means BF16, independently of activation dtype |
+
+## Explicit FP16 configuration
+
+Select both `--dtype float16` and `--kv-cache-dtype float16` for FP16 activations,
+FP16 conv history, and FP16 full-attention K/V storage. Leave
+`--mamba-ssm-dtype float32` for FP32 recurrent state. The corresponding Python
+engine arguments are `dtype="float16"`, `kv_cache_dtype="float16"`, and
+`mamba_ssm_dtype="float32"`.
+
+Setting only `--dtype float16` changes conv history to FP16 but **does not**
+change `auto` KV storage: K/V stays BF16. Explicit `--kv-cache-dtype bfloat16`
+has the same KV storage behavior. BF16 activation configurations preserve the
+previous BF16 conv-history contract.
+
+The Qwen GDN recipe accepts FP16, BF16, and FP32 activation dtypes for conv
+history and rejects other activation dtypes when declaring the state fields.
+This is a planning contract, not a promise that every attention or conv backend
+supports all three types. Backend capability checks still apply. FP32 is not
+added as a KV-cache dtype choice.
+
+## Storage and transfer contracts
+
+FP16 and BF16 both use two bytes per element, but have different encodings.
+Plans and serialized cache-transfer contracts retain the dtype name, not just
+its byte width. Peer validation must reject FP16/BF16 field mismatches even
+when field shapes, strides, and allocation sizes match. Transfer peers need
+compatible activation, SSM, and KV precision settings; equal byte sizes do not
+make their state interchangeable.
+
+FP8 aliases, scatter-backed FP8 byte views, and MXFP8 handling are unchanged.
+In particular, the Qwen GDN recipe still rejects the MXFP8 interleaved scale
+layout. This change does not relax conv validators, add casts, or change any
+kernel implementation.
+
+## CPU regression tests
+
+From the TokenSpeed repository root, in an existing runtime environment with
+PyTorch and pytest installed:
+
+```sh
+PYTHONPATH=python:tokenspeed-kernel/python python -m pytest -q test/runtime/test_qwen35_cache_precision.py
+```
+
+The tests use real attention components, Qwen GDN recipes, group declarations,
+packed memory plans, small CPU cache arenas, and serialized transfer contracts.
+They cover activation/SSM/KV precision independence, unchanged BF16 defaults,
+explicit FP16 CLI and Python arguments, dtype-aware peer rejection, and the
+existing quantized-cache behavior. They do not load weights or run accelerator
+kernels. An actual NPU launch is separate verification; these tests alone do
+not establish end-to-end FP16 model correctness.
